      "finding": "The residual ledger stores an explicit proposition string but not its elaborated proposition and contextual meaning. A later mathematical_claims entry marks it checked solely when the statement string matches. Source-retention guards protect earlier files, but they do not establish that the same text elaborated in a different importing module has the same meaning. Added names/notation/context can differ without replacing retained files. Reuse of the same residual id also compares statement text only.",
      "impact": "The next request and burden report can treat a residual as discharged without a checked bridge to the antecedent of the original reduction. This does not demonstrate false exact-root completion, which has a separate gate.",
      "acceptance": "Bind the residual to the semantic proposition/context used by the checked reduction; admit discharge only with that same identity or an independently checked transport/composition."
    },
