      "finding": "The conditional dictionary is always snapshots/initial. The bundle accumulates every retained root-connected reduction, dependency and discharge; pairs require equal initial-dictionary digest. This measures the cumulative encoding of root-connected witnesses and overhead relative to the initial seed. It does not compare a fixed remaining goal/residual task conditional on old versus newly enlarged accepted theories.",
      "impact": "The measure is a legitimate narrower storage/explicit-witness audit, but cannot be presented as implementing the user's K(goal | new step + previous knowledge) proxy. Accumulating ever more witnesses naturally increases this representation; no decrease or sawtooth should be manufactured to compensate.",
      "acceptance": "Represent each bound theory and a current goal/residual witness conditional on that theory; separately expose new dictionary, gluing/adapter/connecting costs and unknown proof remainder. Keep the mathematical goal/reference panel fixed, charge abbreviation overhead, and make no inference of minimal proof complexity or difficulty from an encoding change."
